%U A399637 2708767626602465,219260081261971868,24145501726791237549,3617974462416349047789,737907391572805636924057,204985716372936815694972161
%N A399637 Number of nonisomorphic right-Euclidean relations on n elements.
%C A399637 Every right-Euclidean relation is a disjoint union of connected components, each having a nonempty reflexive equivalence class, together with isolated nonreflexive elements. Therefore, if c(n) = A399636(n), then the present sequence is obtained from c(n) by an Euler transform, with an additional factor 1/(1-x) for the isolated nonreflexive elements.
%F A399637 G.f.: (1/(1-x))*Product_{n>=1} (1-x^n)^(-A399636(n)).
%e A399637 For n = 3, representatives of the 12 isomorphism classes are {}, {(1,1)}, {(1,1),(2,1)}, {(1,1),(2,2)}, {(1,1),(2,1),(3,1)}, {(1,1),(2,1),(3,3)}, {(1,1),(2,2),(3,3)}, {(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2)}, {(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2),(3,1)}, {(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2),(3,3)}, {(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2),(3,1),(3,2)}, and {(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(3,1),(3,2),(3,3)}.
%Y A399637 Cf. A399636 (connected case), A398718 (labeled case).
